//@ compile-fail
//@ error-contains: `assert_throws` is not implemented
//
// `assert_throws` is parsed as an intrinsic but implemented nowhere below the
// parser. Its argument would have to be a throwing call — rejected by the
// checker outside a `try` — yet a NON-throwing argument used to check fine,
// and lowering turned the assertion into a no-op: `assert_throws(42)`
// compiled and silently passed. An assertion that cannot fail is worse than a
// missing one, so every `assert_throws` is an error until the checker can
// treat its argument as a throw sink (decisions.md, "One process per test").

fn main() {
    assert_throws(42);
}
